+// THIRDLIFE PATCH 0001 (Third Life, lane K8; docs/design/HOCKEY-BALANCE.md): the rule switches of the hockey.thirdlife cartridge. thirdjam's cartridge schema
+// does not know them and no cartridge key reads them: the host fills FJamGameConfig::Tl from <cartridge>.rules.json after the load (TlSetRule, one call
+// a key). Every switch at its default is thirdjam's rule, bit for bit (rink.sh balance-thirdlife --parity plays hockey.regular on this tree against the
+// reference baseline, hash for hash).
+struct FTlRules
+{
+};
+// The host's one entry: sets a switch by its rules.json key. false = an unknown key (the host reports it: unknown keys are errors).
+inline bool TlSetRule(FTlRules& R, const char* Key, double Value)
+{
+	(void)R; (void)Value;
+	const std::string K(Key ? Key : "");
+	// one line per patch, below
+	return false;
+}
